      "case": "textbook_inventory",
      "question": "Which required textbooks support this course? Count distinct textbook titles, give each title and its role, and explain whether every unit assigns all three.",
      "request_mode": "fresh conversation; Canvas delivery; lesson unit-01.html; no learning field",
      "status": 200,
      "content_type": "text/event-stream",
      "answer": "The course's required free reading plan uses **3 distinct textbook titles**, each with a separate role:\n\n| Title | Role in the course |\n|---|---|\n| *Artificial Intelligence: Foundations of Computational Agents*, 3rd ed., by David L. Poole and Alan K. Mackworth (Cambridge University Press) | AI foundation |\n| *Entrepreneurship*, 1st ed., by Michael Laverty and Chris Littel (OpenStax) | Business foundation |\n| *Introductory Statistics 2e*, 2nd ed., by Barbara Illowsky and Susan Dean (OpenStax) | Statistics companion |\n\n**Does every unit assign all three?** No. Each unit assigns only its listed short passages, not the whole of all three books. For example, the Unit 10 and Unit 8 pages each show a \"Required textbook reading\" block with a short time estimate ([Unit 10: Support the first real task](/teaching/ai-solutions/unit-10.html#section-1)). The course material I can see does not name the specific title or passage for each unit's reading, so I can't tell you from here which titles a given unit uses. For a unit-specific answer, count the distinct titles in that unit's current reading metadata. Two sections from one book count as one textbook.\n\n**Important limit:** I have only the course-authored directions and explanations for these readings. I don't have the textbook text itself, so I can't quote the books or give page numbers. If a passage's content matters to your question, paste a short relevant excerpt and I'll explain how it connects to the unit.\n\n**Next step:** Open your current unit's reading in Canvas, note the title and section listed there, and tell me the unit number and the passage you're reading. I'll help you connect that passage to the unit's task.",
      "source_titles": [
        "Unit 1: AI capabilities and useful tasks \u2014 Choose a capability, then inspect its output",
