      "status": 200,
      "content_type": "text/event-stream",
      "answer": "No. I can't read or quote complete textbooks, and I don't have textbook text in my course materials. What I have is course-authored material: which sections to read and where to stop, short explanations of how each section connects to the course, and worked examples. I have no book excerpts, chapters, or page numbers, and I can't claim access to full books.\n\nFor Unit 1, the assigned reading is only the opening of section 1.1 of Poole and Mackworth's *Artificial Intelligence: Foundations of Computational Agents* (3rd edition). Stop at the heading \"1.1.1 Artificial and Natural Intelligence.\" That is the only textbook title assigned in this unit. You can find the scope on the [Unit 1 reading page](/teaching/ai-solutions/unit-01.html#required-reading-heading-1).\n\nFor a question about one paragraph, paste the short passage here. I'll treat it as text you provided, not as something from the course materials. I can then help you:\n- restate the idea in plain language,\n- connect it to your project task, and\n- check whether your reading matches what the passage actually says.\n\nPlease keep pastes to a short passage and leave out confidential information.\n\nYour next step: read the assigned scope in the official reader, then write one idea from it in your own words and name the decision it informs for your project update. Share that with me, and I'll give you feedback.",
